493 0 obj
<<
/Title (The first priority should be high-volume bottlenecks because improvement there can affect the greatest number of shipments. The second priority should be routes with high variability, since inconsistency makes planning difficult. The third priority should be low-volume extreme delays, which may indicate special cases, data quality issues, or remote delivery constraints.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 410 0 R
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Title (Conclusion This project establishes a complete data-driven framework for understanding factory-to-customer shipping efficiency at Nassau Candy Distributor. Through cleaning, feature engineering, EDA, route aggregation, geographic analysis, and dashboard development, raw data becomes a practical decision-support resource. The combined use of Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Excel, VS Code, and Streamlit supports both technical reproducibility and business usability.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 30 0 R
/Prev 411 0 R
/Next 412 0 R
>>
endobj
